  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "The study evaluated the integration of air quality and climate plans across local and regional governance levels in Tuscany, Italy, using a deductive content analysis of municipal planning documents. It identified endogenous drivers (sub-national administrative support and public participation) and exogenous factors (participation in transnational climate networks) that influence policy alignment. The analysis revealed that while municipal governments show strong climate planning ambitions, implementation is constrained by administrative gaps that require improved multi-level policy dialogue and structured participatory frameworks.",
      "why": "It isolates the specific organizational and network factors that prevent municipal climate ambitions from translating into integrated air quality actions within regional governance structures."
    }
